&lt;p&gt;07-Nov-2024 TMF633 v4.0.0 CTK file fix Mac-Linux-RUNCTK.sh modified to remove syntax errors. No impact to awarded Open API Conformance certifications.</td><td>TMF633</td><td>Service</td><td>RESTful</td><td>v4.0</td><td>2026-05-15</td><td>Production</td></tr><tr><td>Service Usage Management API</td><td>&lt;p&gt;The Service Usage Management API provides a standardized mechanism for service usage management such as the creation, update, retrieval, import and export of a collection of service usages.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; 14-Oct-2024 TMF727 v5.0.0 preview release: Open API Specification, User Guide and Conformance profile updates for consistency between Usage APIs: Product Usage, Service Usage and Resource Usage. </td><td>TMF727</td><td>Service</td><td>RESTful</td><td>N/A</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>DCS 5GSlice Service Activation API</td><td>&lt;p title=""&gt;Domain Context Specialization of TMF640 for 5G Service Slice, Swagger of Contract is strongly bound to the GSMA Service Definition&lt;/p&gt;</td><td>TMF924</td><td>Service</td><td>RESTful</td><td>N/A</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Federated ID Management API</td><td>&lt;p&gt;The management of principals of any kind (persons, objects, …) and their access to resources in an open environment which can span across different enterprise boundaries. It relies on authentication, authorization and consent mechanisms to protect privacy with a simple and easy user experience. Different parties can provide identity services (operators, social networks, GSMA, …).&lt;/p&gt;</td><td>TMF691</td><td>Common</td><td>RESTful</td><td>N/A</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Work Qualification Management</td><td>No description available yet</td><td>TMF714</td><td>Common</td><td>RESTful</td><td>N/A</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Incident Management API</td><td>The Incident Management API provides a standardized mechanism to report, diagnose and resolve incidents and manages the entire lifecycle of incidents as defined by ITIL. The primary objective of incident management is to restore normal service operation as quickly as possible and minimize the adverse impact on business operations, ensuring that agreed levels of service quality are maintained.
&lt;p&gt;
v4.0.0 15-May-2026 –  CTK updated
docker-compose has been expanded to enable proxy settings by default, simplifying CTK execution in corporate HTTP proxy environments. README files have been updated to document proxy configuration.&lt;/p&gt;</td><td>TMF724</td><td>Common</td><td>RESTful</td><td>v4.0</td><td>2026-05-15</td><td>Production</td></tr><tr><td>Work Management</td><td>The Work Management API facilitates the management and tracking of various telecom-related work activities (for example installation, maintenance, upgrades, and repairs). It provides endpoints to create, retrieve, update, and delete work-related resources.
&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Version history&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/br&gt;
&lt;p&gt;v5.0.0
&lt;p&gt; 18-Sept-2026  TMF713 v5.0.0 RC1 Preview release: Open API Specification (OAS), User Guide, Conformance profile, and Postman.&lt;/p&gt;</td><td>TMF713</td><td>Business Partner</td><td>RESTful</td><td>N/A</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Resource Activation Management API</td><td>The Resource Activation and Configuration API can be used to query resource instances to acquire the resource activation states and attributes, and it can be used to create/update, configure and activate the resource instances.
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;v5.0.0&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
25-Sept-2026 – TMF702 v5.0.0 RC2 Preview release: Open API Specification (OAS), User Guide, Conformance Profile, and Postman Collection.
&lt;p&gt;
11-Sept-2026 – TMF702 v5.0.0 RC1 Preview release: Open API Specification (OAS), User Guide, Conformance Profile, and Postman Collection.
&lt;p&gt;
V4.0 15-May-2026 –  CTK updated
docker-compose has been expanded to enable proxy settings by default, simplifying CTK execution in corporate HTTP proxy environments. README files have been updated to document proxy configuration.&lt;/p&gt;</td><td>TMF702</td><td>Resource</td><td>RESTful</td><td>v4.0</td><td>2026-05-15</td><td>Production</td></tr><tr><td>Communication Management API</td><td>&lt;p&gt;Provides a capability to create and send communications, notifications, and instructions to Parties, Individuals, Organizations or Users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
V4.0 15-May-2026 –  CTK updated
docker-compose has been expanded to enable proxy settings by default, simplifying CTK execution in corporate HTTP proxy environments. README files have been updated to document proxy configuration.&lt;/p&gt;</td><td>TMF681</td><td>Common</td><td>RESTful</td><td>v4.0</td><td>2026-05-15</td><td>Production</td></tr><tr><td>SLA Management API</td><td>&lt;p&gt;Provides a standardized interface for Service Level Agreement (SLA) life-cycle Management (SLA Negotiation, SLA configuration SLA Activation/enforcement, SLA Operations, SLA violation / consequence handling, SLA reporting) between a Customer and a Service Provider which provides offers (product with attached SLA in its catalogue) the customer can discover, browse, trigger and order.&lt;/p&gt;</td><td>TMF623</td><td>Business Partner</td><td>RESTful</td><td>N/A</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>IoT Agent and Device Management API</td><td>In addition to including established TM Forum Open APIs, such as alarm management, resource management and activation APIs, the IoT Device Management API Component Suite also includes an IoT Data Access Endpoint API. This API allows for IoT data access using different types of protocols (MQTT IoT, CoAP, etc.). It encapsulates the protocols and allows devices to be easily integrated into solutions that support a host of IoT initiatives, including smart cities, smart factories and other vertical markets.</td><td>TMF908</td><td>Resource</td><td>RESTful</td><td>N/A</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Event Management API</td><td>The Event Management API provides a standardized client interface to the enterprise event management system for creating, managing and receiving service related events to (indicatively) drive automation workflows, notify other service providers for service outages and SLA violations, trigger Trouble Ticket creation, and enable more complex orchestration scenarios between management systems. The Event Management API can also be used to convey business level Events in support of other processes.</td><td>TMF688</td><td>Common</td><td>RESTful</td><td>N/A</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Shipping Order Management API</td><td>Provides the necessary functionality to create, update and query Shipping Orders. A Shipping Order is a document used by a business to specify what items are to be transferred from a storage location or warehouse to which person and to which new location. A ShippingOrder typically is sent along with a shipment of goods so that the person receiving them can verify that the document correctly reflects the items that they actually received.</td><td>TMF700</td><td>Business Partner</td><td>RESTful</td><td>N/A</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Test Environment Management API</td><td>This API provides a standardized mechanism for the management of test artefacts related to test environment specification. These include Abstract Test Environments, Concrete Environment Metamodels used to map abstract environments to concrete test resources, Environment Provisioning Artefacts, and Test Resource APIs exposed to test cases.
19 July 2024: CTK fix
&lt;p&gt;
V4.0 15-May-2026 –  CTK updated
docker-compose has been expanded to enable proxy settings by default, simplifying CTK execution in corporate HTTP proxy environments. README files have been updated to document proxy configuration.&lt;/p&gt;</td><td>TMF705</td><td>Common</td><td>RESTful</td><td>v4.0</td><td>2026-05-15</td><td>Production</td></tr><tr><td>Appointment Management API</td><td>&lt;p&gt;An Appointment is an arrangement for service provider personnel to carry out some activity at a particular time and place, typically (but not exclusively) at customer premises. It could be used to install a product service, deliver a product order item or solve a customer problem. This API provides the interface for managing Appointments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Version history&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;p&gt;v5.0.0&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; 12-Aug-2026  TMF646 v5.0.0 RC2 Preview release: Open API Specification (OAS), User Guide, Conformance Profile, and Postman Collection. The `POST /searchTimeSlot` operation has been marked as a task resource, and metadata, including description fields have been updated. &lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;15-July-2026 TMF646 v5.0.0 RC1 Preview release: Open API Specification (OAS), User Guide, Conformance Profile, and Postman Collection. This release provides an updated v5.0.0 preview of the Document Management API, aligned with the latest TM Forum Open API standards and includes a Postman Collection.&lt;/p&gt;

