&lt;/style&gt;</td><td>TMF771</td><td>Resource</td><td>RESTful</td><td>v5.0</td><td>2026-05-08</td><td>Production</td></tr><tr><td>Service Ordering Management API</td><td>&lt;p&gt;The REST API for Service Order Management provides a standardized mechanism for placing a service order with all the necessary order parameters. It allows users to create, update &amp; retrieve Service Orders and manages related notifications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Version history&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;p&gt;v4.2.0&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; 14-Aug-2026  TMF641 v4.2.0 Stable release: Open API Specification (OAS), User Guide, Conformance profile, CTK, VS, and Postman.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; 13-Aug-2026  TMF641 v4.2.0 RC2 Preview release: Open API Specification (OAS), User Guide, and Conformance Profile. This change was adding ServiceOrderSpecification as a managed resource, together with its sub-resources. In addition added clarifications in the user guide on the usage of modifyPath, milestone, and jeopardy attributes within the ServiceOrder resource.&lt;/p&gt; 
01 Aug 2024 v4.2.0 release The changes are made to reflect the updates done in service resource model to align with TMF638 v4.2 and TMF640 v4.2 updates and also the addition of optional modifyPath attribute in serviceOrderItem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;v4.1.0&lt;/br&gt;
&lt;p&gt;15 May 2026 – CTK updated
date query parameters previously required values to be enclosed in double quotes. This has been corrected — dates are now passed unquoted. docker-compose has been expanded to enable proxy settings by default, simplifying CTK execution in corporate HTTP proxy environments. README files have been updated to document proxy configuration. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;12 Mar 2026 TMF641 v4.1.0 release: This update includes fixes and minor improvements to the CTK and Reference Implementation. The update corrects the use of a string for a datetime filter parameter, which has now been aligned to the proper ISO 8601 date-time format. README files have also been improved with clearer guidance, including suggested proxy configuration for Docker images to support testing vendor implementations across different networks. The Docker image tag has been incremented from v1.0.0 to v1.0.1 to reflect this patch update.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;20-Dec-2024: v4.1.0 Updates to CTK and RI released: Removed @type mandatory in RelatedParty for TMF641 Service Order. Note: in general v4.x APIs do not mandate @type
&lt;p&gt;28-Nov-2024: Fix released for CTK. The payload within the test cases was adjusted so that the CTK now correctly passes when pointed to the associated RI.  The CTK test cases were adjusted to remove the double-quotes (") around the orderDate filter and replaced with single-quotes ('). The URL is now /serviceOrder?orderDate='2024-11-12' to make things easier to read. 
&lt;p&gt;07-Nov-2024: TMF641 v4.0.0 CTK file fix Mac-Linux-RUNCTK.sh modified to remove syntax errors. No impact to awarded Open API Conformance certifications.

 </td><td>TMF641</td><td>Service</td><td>RESTful</td><td>v4.2</td><td>2026-08-14</td><td>Production</td></tr><tr><td>Private Optimized Binding</td><td>TMF759 Private Optimized Binding API provides the ability to improve the network connection between user equipment and cloud application by means of a simple switch, creating a new way to improve user experience and open new revenue stream.

&lt;p&gt;TMF759 is derived from TMF702, TMF759 opens the door for future APIs, allowing to manage more dedicated core network operations to bolster NaaS capabilities</td><td>TMF759</td><td>Resource</td><td>RESTful</td><td>N/A</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Performance Management API</td><td>&lt;p&gt;Provides a standardized mechanism for performance management such as the creation, partial or full update and retrieval of resources involved in performance management (Measurement Production Job, Measurement Collection Job, and Ad hoc Collection). It also allows notification of events related to performance. &lt;/p&gt;</td><td>TMF628</td><td>Common</td><td>RESTful</td><td>N/A</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Network as a Service Management API</td><td>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgb(36,41,46);"&gt;The API Component Suite supports of a set of Operational Domains exposing and managing “Network” Services. These services are referred to as Network as a Service (NaaS) and include all services offered from a service provider including connectivity, end points, media services, etc. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
