&lt;/style&gt;</td><td>TMF738</td><td>Business Partner</td><td>RESTful</td><td>v5.0</td><td>2026-05-08</td><td>Production</td></tr><tr><td>Outage Management API</td><td>&lt;p&gt;The Outage Management API enables telecommunications operators to capture, manage, and share network outage and service disruption details with customers, partners, and regulatory bodies. It provides comprehensive information on impacted services, affected regions, estimated restoration times, and historical outage records.
By standardizing outage communication, the API improves customer transparency, supports regulatory compliance, and enhances operational efficiency. Operators can minimize customer frustration, reduce reputational risks, and streamline customer support by making accurate and timely outage details accessible across multiple channels, including websites, portals, and notifications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Version history&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;p&gt; v5.0.0&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;4-September-2025  v5.0.0 preview release with OAS, User Guide and Conformance Profile.&lt;/p&gt;</td><td>TMF777</td><td>Service</td><td>RESTful</td><td>N/A</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Service Test Management API</td><td>&lt;p&gt;The Service Test API provides a standardized mechanism for placing a service test with all the necessary test parameters. The API consists of a simple set of operations that interact with CRM/Service Management systems in a consistent manner. A service test is a procedure intended to check the quality, performance, or reliability of a service.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Version history&lt;/b&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;v5.0.0
&lt;p&gt; 4-Sept-2026  TMF653 v5.0.0  Stable release: Open API Specification (OAS), User Guide, Conformance Profile, Postman Collection, CTK and RI. 
&lt;p&gt; 12-Aug-2026  TMF653 v5.0.0  RC1 Preview release: Open API Specification (OAS), User Guide, Conformance Profile, and Postman Collection. TTMF653 Service Test Management has been updated. The CancelServiceTest resource type has been added, enabling submission and retrieval of service test cancellation requests via POST /cancelServiceTest and GET /cancelServiceTest/{id}, with listener endpoints for create, state change, and information required events. A ServiceTestInformationRequiredEvent listener endpoint has also been added for the existing serviceTest resource. A new GET /hub/{id} operation has been added, and query parameters before, after, sort, and filter have been added to GET /serviceTest and GET /serviceTestSpecification. PATCH responses for /serviceTest/{id} and /serviceTestSpecification/{id} no longer return application/json-patch+json, application/json-patch-query+json, or application/merge-patch+json; only application/json is returned. The ServiceTestSpecRelationship schema has been replaced by ServiceTestRelationship and ServiceTestSpecificationRelationship.
The following schemas have new required fields:
* ServiceTestSpecification (PATCH request body): relatedServiceSpecification
* All ServiceTest*Event and ServiceTestSpecification*Event schemas: event
* ServiceTest*EventPayload schemas: serviceTest; ServiceTestSpecification*EventPayload schemas: serviceTestSpecification
Several shared sub-object schemas also have additional required fields: Attachment (attachmentType, mimeType); AttachmentRef (@referredType); CharacteristicSpecification (name, valueType); CharacteristicSpecificationRelationship (name, parentSpecificationId, relationshipType); EntitySpecification (name); EntitySpecificationRelationship (associationSpec, relationshipType, role, validFor); TargetEntitySchema (@type, @schemaLocation); and all typed *Characteristic schemas (value).&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;
