&lt;/style&gt;</td><td>TMF621</td><td>Common</td><td>RESTful</td><td>v5.0</td><td>2026-05-08</td><td>Production</td></tr><tr><td>Payment Management API</td><td>&lt;p&gt;The Payments API provides the standardized client interface to Payment Systems for notifying about performed payments or refunds. Examples of Payment API originators (clients) include Web servers, mobile app servers, Contact center dashboards or retail store systems. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Version History&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;15 May 2026 – CTK updated
date query parameters previously required values to be enclosed in double quotes. This has been corrected — dates are now passed unquoted. docker-compose has been expanded to enable proxy settings by default, simplifying CTK execution in corporate HTTP proxy environments. README files have been updated to document proxy configuration. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;12 Mar 2026 TMF676 v4.0.0 release: This update includes fixes and minor improvements to the CTK and Reference Implementation.
The update corrects the use of a string for a datetime filter parameter, which has now been aligned to the proper ISO 8601 date-time format. README files have also been improved with clearer guidance, including suggested proxy configuration for Docker images to support testing vendor implementations across different networks.
The Docker image tag has been incremented from v1.0.0 to v1.0.1 to reflect this patch update.&lt;/p&gt;</td><td>TMF676</td><td>Customer</td><td>RESTful</td><td>v4.0</td><td>2026-05-15</td><td>Production</td></tr><tr><td>Usage Consumption Management API</td><td>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgb(51,51,51);"&gt;This API provides the real-time value within buckets (SMS, Voice, Data, TV for example) that a customer consumes with each of their devices, related to subscribed communication products without having to wait for the bill cycle. A usage report retrieves the data related to these balances.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Version history&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;p&gt;v5.1&lt;/pr&gt;
