V4.0 15-May-2026 –  CTK updated
docker-compose has been expanded to enable proxy settings by default, simplifying CTK execution in corporate HTTP proxy environments. README files have been updated to document proxy configuration.&lt;/p&gt;</td><td>TMF709</td><td>Common</td><td>RESTful</td><td>v4.0</td><td>2026-05-15</td><td>Production</td></tr><tr><td>Process Management API</td><td>&lt;p&gt;The Process Management API allows management of business process. It provides all required information to achieve business task requiring manual action:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Version history&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;p&gt;v5.0.0&lt;/pr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
11-Sept-2026 – TMF701 v5.0.0 Stable release: Open API Specification (OAS), User Guide, Conformance Profile, Postman Collection, CTK and RI.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
20-Aug-2026 – TMF701 v5.0.0 RC4 Preview release: Open API Specification (OAS), User Guide, Conformance Profile, and Postman Collection. Minor updates include removing HTTP 404 responses from collection operations, updating all resources to use the most recent schemas, and making the Process DELETE endpoint optional.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
04-Jun-2026 – TMF701 v5.0.0 RC3 Preview release: Open API Specification (OAS), User Guide, Conformance Profile, and Postman Collection. This minor update includes improvements to the User Guide and Conformance Profile. In addition, the &lt;code&gt;@referredType&lt;/code&gt; field on the &lt;code&gt;TaskRef&lt;/code&gt; schema is now marked as mandatory to improve interoperability and consistency across implementations. This release also includes updates to resource naming to improve alignment and simplify the API model, where ProcessFlow has been renamed to Process, ProcessFlowSpecification to ProcessSpecification, TaskFlow to Task, and TaskFlowSpecification to TaskSpecification.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt; 20-May-2026 TMF701 preview release v5.0.0: Open API Specification (OAS), User Guide, Conformance Profile, Postman Collection.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt; 20-Sept-2024 release: OAS v4.1.0 update for: &lt;br&gt;processFlowSpecification attribute (string) of ProcessFlow resource : change it from required (in the POST) to optional. This is backward compatible change.  Conformance profile is now compatible with the swagger.
 </td><td>TMF701</td><td>Common</td><td>RESTful</td><td>v5.0</td><td>2026-09-11</td><td>Production</td></tr><tr><td>Resource Inventory Management API</td><td>&lt;p&gt;
The intent of this API is to provide a consistent and standardized mechanism to query and manipulate the Resource inventory.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Version history&lt;/b&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;v5.0.0&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; 08-May-2026 docker-compose has been expanded to enable proxy settings by default, simplifying CTK execution in corporate HTTP proxy environments where this previously required in‑house configuration. README files have been updated to document proxy usage. Failed HTML reports can now be opened directly in a browser, and HTML reports now include headers identifying the API and CTK version used, improving certification clarity and traceability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
08-Apr-2026 – TMF639 v5.0.0 Stable release: Open API Specification (OAS), User Guide, Conformance Profile, Postman Collection, CTK and RI
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
20-Mar-2026 – TMF639 v5.0.0 RC2 Preview release: Open API Specification (OAS), User Guide, Conformance Profile, and Postman Collection. 
Includes a fix addressing misalignment between the Conformance Profile and OAS for &lt;code&gt;supportingResource&lt;/code&gt;. The Conformance Profile previously marked &lt;code&gt;@referredType&lt;/code&gt; as mandatory, while the OAS defines &lt;code&gt;supportingResource&lt;/code&gt; using a polymorphic &lt;code&gt;oneOf&lt;/code&gt; (Resource or ResourceRef), where &lt;code&gt;@referredType&lt;/code&gt; is not consistently required. This update aligns the definitions to ensure consistency across assets.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
11-Mar-2026 – TMF639 v5.0.0 RC1 Preview release: Open API Specification (OAS), User Guide, Conformance Profile, and Postman Collection.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;v4.0.0&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
