15-May-2026 –  CTK updated
docker-compose has been expanded to enable proxy settings by default, simplifying CTK execution in corporate HTTP proxy environments. README files have been updated to document proxy configuration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
07-Nov-2024 – TMF639 v4.0.0 CTK file fix: Mac-Linux-RUNCTK.sh modified to remove syntax errors. No impact to awarded Open API Conformance certifications.
&lt;/p&gt;</td><td>TMF639</td><td>Resource</td><td>RESTful</td><td>v4.0</td><td>2026-05-15</td><td>Production</td></tr><tr><td>Geographic Site Management API</td><td>&lt;p&gt;Covers the operations to manage (create, read, delete) sites that can be associated with a customer, account, service delivery or other entities. This API defines a Site as a convenience class that allows easy reference to places important to other entities, where a geographic place is an entity that can answer the question “where?”&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Version history&lt;/b&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;v5.0.0&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
05-Aug-2026 – TMF674 v5.0.0 Stable release including the Open API Specification (OAS), User Guide, Conformance Profile, Postman Collection, Sample Implementation Code, and Conformance Test Kit (CTK).
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; 20-May-2026 TMF674 v5.0.0-rc.2: Updated to reflect that fields marked as required in schemas should also be included in response payloads to provide a meaningful representation of the resource for validation and integrations. Be aware that some formerly optional fields are now correctly marked as required in this release.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
08-Apr-2026 –TMF674 v5.0.0-rc.2 :Make referredType required on the AttachmentRef schema to enable polymorphic support in a wider selection of tools.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
31-Mar-2026 TMF674 v5.0.0 preview release: Open API Specification, User Guide, Postman Collection, and Conformance Profile.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
V4.0 15-May-2026 –  CTK updated
docker-compose has been expanded to enable proxy settings by default, simplifying CTK execution in corporate HTTP proxy environments. README files have been updated to document proxy configuration.&lt;/p&gt;</td><td>TMF674</td><td>Common</td><td>RESTful</td><td>v4.0</td><td>2026-05-15</td><td>Production</td></tr><tr><td>Geographic Address Management API</td><td>&lt;p&gt;Provides a standardized client interface to an Address management system. It allows looking for worldwide addresses. It can also be used to validate geographic address data, to be sure that it corresponds to a real geographic address. Finally, it can be used to look for a geographic address by: searching an area as a start (city, town ...), then zooming on the streets of this area, and finally listing all the street segments (numbers) in a street.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Version history&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;15 May 2026 – v4.0.0 CTK updated
date query parameters previously required values to be enclosed in double quotes. This has been corrected — dates are now passed unquoted. docker-compose has been expanded to enable proxy settings by default, simplifying CTK execution in corporate HTTP proxy environments. README files have been updated to document proxy configuration. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;12 Mar 2026 TMF673 v4.0.0 release: This update includes fixes and minor improvements to the CTK and Reference Implementation.
The update corrects the use of a string for a datetime filter parameter, which has now been aligned to the proper ISO 8601 date-time format. README files have also been improved with clearer guidance, including suggested proxy configuration for Docker images to support testing vendor implementations across different networks.
The Docker image tag has been incremented from v1.0.0 to v1.0.1 to reflect this patch update.&lt;/p&gt;
</td><td>TMF673</td><td>Common</td><td>RESTful</td><td>v4.0</td><td></td><td>Production</td></tr><tr><td>Dunning Case Management</td><td>&lt;p&gt;The Dunning Case Management API enables systems to identify, track, and manage outstanding debts resulting from payment refusal or delay. It supports automated recovery through defined strategies, including service suppression.
 &lt;/p&gt;
