&lt;p&gt;07-Nov-2024 TMF648 v4.0.0 CTK file fix Mac-Linux-RUNCTK.sh modified to remove syntax errors. No impact to awarded Open API Conformance certifications.</td><td>TMF648</td><td>Customer</td><td>RESTful</td><td>v4.0</td><td>2026-05-15</td><td>Production</td></tr><tr><td>Resource Portability API</td><td>The TMF689 Resource Portability API provides a standardized mechanism for managing the portability of telecommunications  resources (such as telephone numbers, network identifiers, and service-related resources) between service providers.
 
&lt;p&gt;This API enables service providers to exchange portability requests in a consistent and interoperable manner, supporting  regulatory requirements for number portability and resource transfer scenarios.
 
&lt;p&gt;Key features include: - Creation and management of portability orders with complete lifecycle tracking - Multi-party coordination between donor (losing) and recipient (gaining) service providers - Customer authorization validation and tracking - Support for both individual and bulk portability requests - Real-time state change notifications for order progress tracking - Flexible activation modes (automatic or manual) for coordinated resource cutover - Comprehensive error handling and information request mechanisms - Cancellation workflows for in-progress portability orders
 
&lt;p&gt;The API integrates with TMF639 Resource Inventory, TMF632 Party Management, TMF673 Geographic Address Management,  and TMF641 Service Ordering to provide end-to-end portability management capabilities.
&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Version history&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;p&gt;v5.0.0&lt;/pr&gt;
16-Oct-2026 – TMF689 v5.0.0 Stable release: Open API Specification (OAS), User Guide, Conformance Profile, CTK, RI, and Postman Collection.
