&lt;p&gt;
V4.0 15-May-2026 –  CTK updated
docker-compose has been expanded to enable proxy settings by default, simplifying CTK execution in corporate HTTP proxy environments. README files have been updated to document proxy configuration.&lt;/p&gt;</td><td>TMF663</td><td>Customer</td><td>RESTful</td><td>v5.0</td><td>2026-05-08</td><td>Production</td></tr><tr><td>Resource Catalog Management API</td><td>&lt;p&gt;The Resource Catalog Management API REST specification allows the management of the entire lifecycle of the Resource Catalog elements and the consultation of resource catalog elements during several processes such as ordering process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Version history&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;br&gt; v5.0.0
&lt;p&gt; 08-May-2026 docker-compose has been expanded to enable proxy settings by default, simplifying CTK execution in corporate HTTP proxy environments where this previously required in‑house configuration. README files have been updated to document proxy usage. Failed HTML reports can now be opened directly in a browser, and HTML reports now include headers identifying the API and CTK version used, improving certification clarity and traceability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;21-Jan-2026 The CTK and RI have been re-released in a dockerized format, this may require different set up requirements and any automation platforms will need to be updated. Click &lt;a href="https://projects.tmforum.org/wiki/display/API/TM+Forum+Open+API+Conformance+Testing+and+Validation+Instructions+Page" 
     target="_blank" 
     rel="noopener noreferrer" 
     class="styled-link"&gt;
    here for more information&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;br&gt; v4.1.0 
&lt;p&gt;15 May 2026 – CTK updated
date query parameters previously required values to be enclosed in double quotes. This has been corrected — dates are now passed unquoted. docker-compose has been expanded to enable proxy settings by default, simplifying CTK execution in corporate HTTP proxy environments. README files have been updated to document proxy configuration. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;12 Mar 2026 TMF634 v4.1.0 release: This update includes fixes and minor improvements to the CTK and Reference Implementation. The update corrects the use of a string for a datetime filter parameter, which has now been aligned to the proper ISO 8601 date-time format. README files have also been improved with clearer guidance, including suggested proxy configuration for Docker images to support testing vendor implementations across different networks. The Docker image tag has been incremented from v1.0.0 to v1.0.1 to reflect this patch update.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;07-Nov-2024 TMF634  CTK file fix Mac-Linux-RUNCTK.sh modified to remove syntax errors. No impact to awarded Open API Conformance certifications.

