&lt;/style&gt;</td><td>TMF634</td><td>Resource</td><td>RESTful</td><td>v5.0</td><td>2026-05-08</td><td>Production</td></tr><tr><td>Entity Catalog Management API</td><td>&lt;p&gt;The entity catalog is intended to provide any SID entity to consumers via a catalog, with its specification and policy providing governance over its content. The API provides management of the entity specifications and their associations through CRUD operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Version history&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/br&gt;
&lt;br&gt;v4.0.0 &lt;/br&gt;
&lt;p&gt;15 May 2026 – CTK updated
date query parameters previously required values to be enclosed in double quotes. This has been corrected — dates are now passed unquoted. docker-compose has been expanded to enable proxy settings by default, simplifying CTK execution in corporate HTTP proxy environments. README files have been updated to document proxy configuration. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;12 Mar 2026 TMF662 v4.0.0 release: This update includes fixes and minor improvements to the CTK and Reference Implementation.
The update corrects the use of a string for a datetime filter parameter, which has now been aligned to the proper ISO 8601 date-time format. README files have also been improved with clearer guidance, including suggested proxy configuration for Docker images to support testing vendor implementations across different networks.
The Docker image tag has been incremented from v1.0.0 to v1.0.1 to reflect this patch update.&lt;/p&gt;

07-Nov-2024 TMF662 v4.0.0 CTK file fix Mac-Linux-RUNCTK.sh modified to remove syntax errors. No impact to awarded Open API Conformance certifications.</td><td>TMF662</td><td>Common</td><td>RESTful</td><td>v4.0</td><td>2026-05-15</td><td>Production</td></tr><tr><td>Account Management API</td><td>&lt;p&gt;Provides standardized mechanism for the management of billing and settlement accounts, as well as for financial accounting (account receivable) either in B2B or B2B2C contexts&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Version history&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;p&gt;v5.0.0&lt;/pr&gt;
&lt;p&gt; 08-May-2026 docker-compose has been expanded to enable proxy settings by default, simplifying CTK execution in corporate HTTP proxy environments where this previously required in‑house configuration. README files have been updated to document proxy usage. Failed HTML reports can now be opened directly in a browser, and HTML reports now include headers identifying the API and CTK version used, improving certification clarity and traceability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;14-Apr-2026 Fixed the oneOf validation logic for BillPresentationMediaRefOrValue and BillFormatRefOrValue schemas when provided payloads matched both branches due to shared inherited properties.&lt;/pr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;08-Apr-2026 Updated CTK filtering behavior to use evaluable scalar fields instead of object-level query parameters.
Resolve filter placeholders dynamically from saved POST response data, including nested field paths.&lt;/pr&gt;
