&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Version history&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;p&gt;v5.0.0 &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; 08-May-2026 docker-compose has been expanded to enable proxy settings by default, simplifying CTK execution in corporate HTTP proxy environments where this previously required in‑house configuration. README files have been updated to document proxy usage. Failed HTML reports can now be opened directly in a browser, and HTML reports now include headers identifying the API and CTK version used, improving certification clarity and traceability.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;31-Mar-2026 – TMF645 v5.0.0 Updated coversheet for User Guide and Conformance Profile.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;17-Mar-2026 – TMF645 v5.0.0 Stable release: Open API Specification (OAS), User Guide, Conformance Profile, Postman Collection, CTK, and Sample implementation code.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;v5.0.0 RC2&lt;/p&gt;
03-March-2026 – TMF645 v5.0.0 RC2 Preview release: Open API Specification (OAS), User Guide, Conformance Profile, and Postman Collection. Includes a fix for a problem where identical &lt;code&gt;oneOf&lt;/code&gt; schemas in the &lt;code&gt;PartyRefOrPartyRoleRef&lt;/code&gt; schema were causing ambiguity. Adding a restriction on the allowed value of &lt;code&gt;@type&lt;/code&gt; allows the API to be used with a wider range of tools without altering the API signatures.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;v5.0.0 rc1&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
12-February-2026 TMF645 v5.0.0 RC1 Preview release with Open API Specification (OAS), User Guide, Conformance Profile, and Postman Collection. 
Includes schema alignment updates, rules.yaml refinements, sample payload corrections, clarification of date attributes, and schema reference corrections.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;v5.0.0&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;4-September-2025  v5.0.0 updated preview release with OAS, User Guide and Conformance Profile, update to current API v5 standards, add missing floatCharacteristic, correct filter parameters, adjust schemas to follow established patterns.&lt;/p&gt;
14-Nov-2024 TMF645 v5.0.0  OAS and User Guide fix for missing Characteristic subclasses in OAS/user guide &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;v4.0.0&lt;/br&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
15-May-2026 –  CTK updated
docker-compose has been expanded to enable proxy settings by default, simplifying CTK execution in corporate HTTP proxy environments. README files have been updated to document proxy configuration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;07-Nov-2024 TMF645 v4.0.0 CTK file fix Mac-Linux-RUNCTK.sh modified to remove syntax errors. No impact to awarded Open API Conformance certifications.</td><td>TMF645</td><td>Service</td><td>RESTful</td><td>v5.0</td><td>2026-05-08</td><td>Production</td></tr><tr><td>Product Usage Catalog Management API</td><td>&lt;p&gt;
TMF767 Product Usage Catalog Management API provides a standardised mechanism for usage management such as creation, update, retrieval, import and export of a collection of product usage. A Product Usage represents an occurrence of usage on a Product derived from various Service usages, which can be further used to generate interest to a billing system, and can have charges applied to it.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
It is comprised of characteristics which define all attributes known for a particular type of Product Usage.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Version history&lt;/b&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;v5.0.0 &lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; 08-May-2026 docker-compose has been expanded to enable proxy settings by default, simplifying CTK execution in corporate HTTP proxy environments where this previously required in‑house configuration. README files have been updated to document proxy usage. Failed HTML reports can now be opened directly in a browser, and HTML reports now include headers identifying the API and CTK version used, improving certification clarity and traceability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;31-Mar-2026 – TMF767 v5.0.0 Updated coversheet for User Guide and Conformance Profile.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;17-Mar-2026 – TMF767 v5.0.0 Stable release: Open API Specification (OAS), User Guide, Conformance Profile, Postman Collection, CTK, and Sample implementation code.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;v5.0.0 RC3&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
03-March-2026 – TMF767 v5.0.0 RC3 Preview release: Open API Specification (OAS), User Guide, Conformance Profile, and Postman Collection. Includes a fix for a problem where identical &lt;code&gt;oneOf&lt;/code&gt; schemas in the &lt;code&gt;PartyRefOrPartyRoleRef&lt;/code&gt; schema were causing ambiguity. Adding a restriction on the allowed value of &lt;code&gt;@type&lt;/code&gt; allows the API to be used with a wider range of tools without altering the API signatures.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;v5.0.0 rc1&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
13-February-2026 TMF767 v5.0.0 rc1 preview release: Open API Specification (OAS), User Guide, Conformance Profile, and Postman Collection. Includes schema updates to ProductUsageSpecification, added Product and Service Usage specification references, removed unused attributes, replaced targetEntitySchema with targetProductUsageSchema, and made name and lifecycleStatus mandatory for create operations.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;v5.0.0&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
14-Oct-2024 TMF767 v5.0.0 preview release: Open API Specification, User Guide and Conformance Profile updates for consistency between Usage APIs: Product Usage, Service Usage and Resource Usage.
&lt;/p&gt;</td><td>TMF767</td><td>Product</td><td>RESTful</td><td>v5.0</td><td>2026-05-08</td><td>Production</td></tr><tr><td>Resource Order Management API</td><td>&lt;p&gt;
The REST API for Resource Order Management. It includes the model definition as well as all available operations. Possible actions are creating, updating and retrieving Resource Orders (including filtering). A Resource Order API provides a standard mechanism for placing a Resource Order with all necessary order parameters.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Version history&lt;/b&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;v5.0.0&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
04-Jun-2026 – TMF652 v5.0.0 RC3 Preview release: Open API Specification (OAS), User Guide, Conformance Profile, and Postman Collection. 
This updated preview includes minor improvements: the &lt;code&gt;@referredType&lt;/code&gt; field is now mandatory in the &lt;code&gt;ResourceRef&lt;/code&gt; schema to improve interoperability, and outdated references to non-existent fields have been removed from the rules and conformance files to ensure consistency across assets.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
20-May-2026 TMF652 v5.0.0 RC1 Preview release: Updated to reflect that fields marked as required in schemas should also be included in response payloads to provide a meaningful representation of the resource for validation and integrations. Be aware that some formerly optional fields are now correctly marked as required in this release.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
10-Apr-2026 – TMF652 v5.0.0 RC1 Preview release: Open API Specification (OAS), User Guide, Conformance Profile and Postman collection.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;v4.0.0&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;15 May 2026 – CTK updated
date query parameters previously required values to be enclosed in double quotes. This has been corrected — dates are now passed unquoted. docker-compose has been expanded to enable proxy settings by default, simplifying CTK execution in corporate HTTP proxy environments. README files have been updated to document proxy configuration. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
12-Mar-2026 – TMF652 v4.0.0 release: This update includes fixes and minor improvements to the CTK and Reference Implementation.
The update corrects the use of a string for a datetime filter parameter, which has now been aligned to the proper ISO 8601 date-time format. README files have also been improved with clearer guidance, including suggested proxy configuration for Docker images to support testing vendor implementations across different networks.
The Docker image tag has been incremented from v1.0.0 to v1.0.1 to reflect this patch update.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
</td><td>TMF652</td><td>Resource</td><td>RESTful</td><td>v4.0</td><td>2026-05-15</td><td>Production</td></tr><tr><td>Intent Management API</td><td>&lt;p&gt;This API allows intents to be expressed, reporting on and negotiated between the intent owner and the intent handler. The Intent API provides specifies the basic attributes and relationships that describe an Intent. The expression attribute of Intent contains a statement of the expectations for an intent in a particular ontology language and is validated by the TM Forum Intent Ontology (TIO).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Version history&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;p&gt;v5.0.0&lt;/pr&gt;
&lt;p&gt; 08-May-2026 docker-compose has been expanded to enable proxy settings by default, simplifying CTK execution in corporate HTTP proxy environments where this previously required in‑house configuration. README files have been updated to document proxy usage. Failed HTML reports can now be opened directly in a browser, and HTML reports now include headers identifying the API and CTK version used, improving certification clarity and traceability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;17-Apr-2026 Fixed test ordering in the CTK, DELETE Intent now runs after all IntentReport tests to prevent sub-resource tests failing with 404.
IntentReport endpoints in the RI now return 404 when the parent Intent does not exist, enforcing referential integrity.&lt;/pr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;21-Jan-2026 The CTK and RI have been re-released in a dockerized format, this may require different set up requirements and any automation platforms will need to be updated. Click &lt;a href="https://projects.tmforum.org/wiki/display/API/TM+Forum+Open+API+Conformance+Testing+and+Validation+Instructions+Page" 
     target="_blank" 
     rel="noopener noreferrer" 
     class="styled-link"&gt;
    here for more information&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;02-Oct-2024 release: v5.0.0 CTK, RI, Postman released. Stable release.

