&lt;p&gt;
17-Mar-2026 – TMF635 v5.0.0 Stable release: Open API Specification (OAS), User Guide, Conformance Profile, Postman Collection, CTK, and Sample implementation code.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
03-Mar-2026 – TMF635 v5.0.0 RC3 Preview release: Open API Specification (OAS), User Guide, Conformance Profile, and Postman Collection. Includes a fix addressing ambiguity caused by identical &lt;code&gt;oneOf&lt;/code&gt; schemas in the &lt;code&gt;PartyRefOrPartyRoleRef&lt;/code&gt; definition. A restriction has been added to the allowed value of &lt;code&gt;@type&lt;/code&gt; to improve tooling compatibility without altering the API signatures.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
22-Jan-2026 – Usage API v4 uplifted to Product Usage v5, aligning the API and schemas with updated design standards. The &lt;code&gt;/usage&lt;/code&gt; endpoint was renamed to &lt;code&gt;/productUsage&lt;/code&gt;. &lt;code&gt;serviceUsage&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;resourceUsage&lt;/code&gt; are now handled by separate APIs (TMF727 and TMF771 respectively). Specifications are managed by the TMF767 Product Usage Catalog Management API. A new &lt;code&gt;/exportJob&lt;/code&gt; resource was introduced to enable file-based export of product usage data, along with corresponding exportJob events.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;v4.0.0&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
15-May-2026 –  CTK updated
docker-compose has been expanded to enable proxy settings by default, simplifying CTK execution in corporate HTTP proxy environments. README files have been updated to document proxy configuration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
