&lt;/style&gt;</td><td>TMF737</td><td>Business Partner</td><td>RESTful</td><td>v5.0</td><td>2026-05-08</td><td>Production</td></tr><tr><td>Customer360 Management API</td><td>An API to give a consolidated Customer overview. This is a view-only API, based on the various underlying involved TM Forum Open APIs. This API provides references where one can find detailed information for: Account, Agreement, Appointment, CustomerBill, InteractionItem, LoyaltyBalance, ProductOrder, ProductValue, Promotion, Quote, ServiceProblem, TroubleTicket, UsageSpecification&lt;p&gt;
Release history&lt;/br&gt;
v5.0.1&lt;/&lt;br&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
11-Sept-2026 – TMF717 Customer 360 API v5.0.1 Stable release: Open API Specification (OAS), User Guide, Conformance Profile, CTK, Postman Collection, and RI. 
&lt;p&gt;
20-Aug-2026 – TMF717 Customer 360 API v5.0.1 RC2 Preview release: Open API Specification (OAS), User Guide, Conformance Profile, and Postman Collection. Minor changes from the previous release candidate include updating the HourPeriod schema with &lt;code&gt;startHour&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;endHour&lt;/code&gt; properties, and replacing the &lt;code&gt;initialized&lt;/code&gt; AppointmentStateType value with &lt;code&gt;expired&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;inProgress&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;pending&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;rescheduled&lt;/code&gt;. For event notification request bodies, &lt;code&gt;engagedParty&lt;/code&gt; is now required on the customer object, &lt;code&gt;state&lt;/code&gt; is required on the productOrder object, and &lt;code&gt;@referredType&lt;/code&gt; is required in ResourceRef.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
08-May-2026 – TMF717 v5.0.1 RC1 Preview release: Open API Specification (OAS), User Guide, Conformance Profile, and Postman Collection.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
This Preview release fixes invalid examples caused by a recent OAS tooling change that made the &lt;code&gt;customer&lt;/code&gt; field mandatory within &lt;code&gt;event.customer360&lt;/code&gt;. A minimal illustrative example was added to satisfy this requirement.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;b&gt;No Customer360 data models were updated in this release.
&lt;br&gt; 01-Nov-2024 v5.0.1 release: preview release fixes to Conformance profile and User Guides. &lt;br&gt; - Updated Acknowledgement Section.
&lt;br&gt; - Corrected create event example.
&lt;br&gt; 20-Sept-2024 v5.0.1 release: OAS hotfix v5.0.1
&lt;br&gt; - Corrected the discrepancies between the parameter names of entity and sub-entity
&lt;br&gt; - Added Loyalty Account in place of Loyalty Balance sub-entity
&lt;br&gt; - Run the specmatic tool on generated oas file and corrected all the errors</td><td>TMF717</td><td>Customer</td><td>RESTful</td><td>v5.0</td><td>2026-09-11</td><td>Production</td></tr><tr><td>Product Ordering Management API</td><td>&lt;p title=""&gt;Provides a standardized mechanism for placing a product order with all the necessary order parameters. The API consists of a simple set of operations that interact with CRM/Order negotiation systems in a consistent manner. A product order is created based on a product offering that is defined in a catalog. The product offering identifies the product or set of products that are available to a customer and includes characteristics such as pricing, product options and market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Version history&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;br&gt; v5.0.0
&lt;p&gt; 08-May-2026 docker-compose has been expanded to enable proxy settings by default, simplifying CTK execution in corporate HTTP proxy environments where this previously required in‑house configuration. README files have been updated to document proxy usage. Failed HTML reports can now be opened directly in a browser, and HTML reports now include headers identifying the API and CTK version used, improving certification clarity and traceability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;21-Jan-2026 The CTK and RI have been re-released in a dockerized format, this may require different set up requirements and any automation platforms will need to be updated. Click &lt;a href="https://projects.tmforum.org/wiki/display/API/TM+Forum+Open+API+Conformance+Testing+and+Validation+Instructions+Page" 
     target="_blank" 
     rel="noopener noreferrer" 
     class="styled-link"&gt;
    here for more information&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;br&gt; v4.0.0 
&lt;p&gt;
15-May-2026 –  CTK updated
docker-compose has been expanded to enable proxy settings by default, simplifying CTK execution in corporate HTTP proxy environments. README files have been updated to document proxy configuration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;07-Nov-2024 TMF622 v4.0.0 CTK file fix Mac-Linux-RUNCTK.sh modified to remove syntax errors. No impact to awarded Open API Conformance certifications.

&lt;style&gt;
